<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  THE SEARCH FIELD. Filters in place; it never navigates.
  32-master-plan-android.md 8.15, 22-components.md 4, D-7.
  ============================================================================

  Radius 16 like every other control (D-7 retires bg_search_pill's 14), fill
  colorSurfaceContainerHighest, 56 as a MINIMUM height so the field and a list row
  share one rhythm and the box grows at a 200% font scale instead of clipping.

  The trailing clear affordance appears only when the field is non-empty — that is
  what endIconMode="clear_text" in the style buys, with Material's own glyph and its
  own content description, so there is no icon-only control here without a name.

  BEHAVIOUR THE CALLER OWNS (8.15):
      debounce 150ms, then filter in place. Never a screen, never a dialog.
      the empty result is a DESIGNED state (view_empty_state.xml: «Ничего не найдено»
        / «Попробуйте другой запрос.» / «Сбросить поиск»), never a blank list.
      the field keeps its text AND its focus when the result is empty.
      Back with a non-empty query clears the query before it leaves the screen.
      searchInput.setHint(...) for a list that is not the server list.

  TWO DEVIATIONS FROM THE STYLE, BOTH DELIBERATE AND BOTH FILED:
  1. app:errorEnabled="false". Widget.Departament.TextField reserves a helper line
     under every field so a form never jumps when a validation message appears. A
     search box has no validation, so on this one control that reservation is dead
     space above the list. The styles owner is asked to fold this into
     Widget.Departament.TextField.Search itself.
  2. No leading glyph. The style's own comment records it: there is no ic_search in
     res/drawable yet, and pointing app:startIconDrawable at ic_outline_filter_alt_24
     would put a filter funnel on a search box. The hint carries the affordance until
     the icon lands, at which point add app:startIconDrawable + app:startIconSize.
-->
<com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout
    xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:id="@+id/search_field"
    style="@style/Widget.Departament.TextField.Search"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="wrap_content"
    app:errorEnabled="false">

    <com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputEditText
        android:id="@+id/search_input"
        android:layout_width="match_parent"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:hint="@string/search_hint"
        android:imeOptions="actionSearch"
        android:inputType="text"
        android:maxLines="1"
        android:singleLine="true"
        tools:text="Amsterdam" />
</com.google.android.material.textfield.TextInputLayout>
